# Refuse to install when the running Node does not satisfy engines.node (">=26").
# Without this npm only warns (EBADENGINE) and installs anyway, which has twice
# produced a silently broken tree on Node 20:
#   1. npm 10 rewrites package-lock.json with every `libc` field stripped, losing
#      the glibc-vs-musl hints the standalone Docker build relies on.
#   2. `next dev` then crashes three dependencies deep with
#      "webidl.util.markAsUncloneable is not a function" — undici 8 (via jsdom,
#      via isomorphic-dompurify, via src/lib/security-utils.ts) reads a
#      node:worker_threads symbol that only exists on Node >= 22.19.
# A loud failure at install time is cheaper than either.
#
# Verified no-op where it matters: exits 0 on Node 26 (CI pins node-version 26,
# Dockerfile is node:26-alpine); exits 1 on Node 20 naming the unmet range.
# npm only enforces the `node`/`npm` engine keys, so the `pnpm` engine declared
# by @socialgouv/matomo-next is ignored.
engine-strict=true
